===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|schīze}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*skītaz}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*skei-d-||to part}}. Indo-European cognates include Ancient Greek {{m|grc|σχιστός}} and English {{m|en|shit}}, German Low German {{m|nds|Schiet}}, Dutch {{m|nl|schijt}}, Frisian {{m|fy|skyt}}, Swedish {{m|sv|skit}} within Germanic. Low German cognates sometimes used in standard German are {{m|de|Schiet}} and {{m|de|Schitte}}.

